---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import coverage from '../data/coverage.json';
import { REPO } from '../lib/site';

const rows = coverage.rows;
const ranDate = (coverage.generated || '').slice(0, 10);
const SAPIS = ['cli', 'fpm', 'apache'] as const;
const SAPI_LABEL: Record<string, string> = { cli: 'CLI server', fpm: 'php-fpm', apache: 'Apache mod_php' };

// Map a per-SAPI cell to a display {pill class, label}. State comes straight
// from the generated data; nothing here invents a verdict.
function cell(sapi: any) {
  if (!sapi || sapi.state === 'none') return { cls: 'na', label: 'not tested' };
  if (sapi.state === 'pass') return { cls: 'ok', label: 'blocked' };
  if (sapi.state === 'skip') return { cls: 'na', label: 'skipped' };
  if (sapi.state === 'fail') return { cls: 'no', label: 'FAILED' };
  return { cls: 'na', label: sapi.state };
}
---
<Layout
  title="Coverage — what Howdah has actually been tested against"
  description="The Howdah test matrix: for every PHP version and server type, whether an upload/part flood was blocked, skipped, or not run. Generated from the lab results, never hand-typed."
  path="/coverage/"
>
  <div class="pagehead">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / <span aria-current="page">Coverage</span></p>
      <h1>Coverage: what has actually been tested</h1>
      <p class="lede">Every cell on this page is generated from the lab test matrix{ranDate && <> (run {ranDate})</>}, never typed by hand. A version is only called &ldquo;blocked&rdquo; where the test for that exact version and server type passed.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="totals" role="group" aria-label="Test totals">
        <div><strong>{coverage.totals.pass}</strong><span>checks passed</span></div>
        <div><strong>{coverage.totals.fail}</strong><span>failed</span></div>
        <div><strong>{coverage.totals.skip}</strong><span>skipped</span></div>
        <div><strong>{coverage.corpusFalsePositives}</strong><span>false positives in the legitimate-upload corpus</span></div>
      </div>

      <h2>By PHP version and server type</h2>
      <p>The two flood shapes tested are a <strong>file-part flood</strong> (<code>max_files</code>) and a <strong>field/part flood</strong> (<code>max_parts</code>). &ldquo;Blocked&rdquo; means the shaped request got HTTP 403 and a log entry at the default limits, on a server with raised caps (the exposed setup). The same runs also sent seven ordinary uploads; none was blocked.</p>
      <div class="tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Coverage by PHP version and server type (scrolls sideways on narrow screens)">
        <table>
          <caption class="sr-only">Per-version, per-server-type coverage</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">PHP</th>
              {SAPIS.map((s) => <th scope="col">{SAPI_LABEL[s]}</th>)}
              <th scope="col">Notes</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {rows.map((r: any) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">{r.version ?? r.minor}</th>
                {r.version ? (
                  <>
                    {SAPIS.map((s) => {
                      const c = cell(r.sapis?.[s]);
                      return <td><span class={`pill ${c.cls}`}>{c.label}</span></td>;
                    })}
                    <td><small style="margin:0">{SAPIS.map((s) => r.sapis?.[s]?.note).filter(Boolean).join('; ')}</small></td>
                  </>
                ) : (
                  <>
                    <td colspan="3"><span class="pill na">not run</span></td>
                    <td><small style="margin:0">{r.why}</small></td>
                  </>
                )}
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="legend">Totals: {coverage.totals.pass} passed, {coverage.totals.fail} failed, {coverage.totals.skip} skipped. Generated by <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/site/scripts/gen-coverage.mjs`}>a script</a> from <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/lab/integration/matrix-results.tsv`}>the raw matrix results</a>. The same data in prose is in <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/docs/coverage.md`}>docs/coverage.md</a>.</p>

      <div class="note">
        <h3>Honest limits of this table</h3>
        <ul class="facts">
          <li>Apache <code>mod_php</code> was tested on the versions whose cell says so (7.4 and 8.1); for others the non-CLI check was php-fpm.</li>
          <li>PHP 5.4 was tested on PHP's built-in server only (its php-fpm column is skipped — no <code>cgi-fcgi</code> in the 5.4 image).</li>
          <li>{coverage.notRunMinors.length} minors were not independently run: {coverage.notRunMinors.join(', ')}. They share a generation's code path with a version that passed — a reason to expect they work, not a test result, and <strong>not</strong> claimed as passing.</li>
          <li>The CVE's <code>session.upload_progress</code> header-parsing path was <strong>not</strong> reproduced. Upload-progress on and off were both tested, to confirm Howdah works either way.</li>
          <li><strong>CVE-2012-1823 (php-cgi argument injection) is out of reach and not protected:</strong> that query is consumed by php-cgi during its own startup, before any PHP extension loads. It belongs with CVE-2019-11043 — both happen before extension code runs. Use a web-server or front-proxy rule.</li>
          <li>The input-shape and request-header limits are enforced best-effort on the response (the variable is always dropped and logged; the 403 may arrive at request shutdown on lazy-superglobal SAPIs). See <a href="/docs/configuration/">Configuration</a>.</li>
          <li>Layer 2 (input inspection) is not covered by this table and is not in a published release yet; it arrives in the next release. It detects and logs SQL injection, path traversal and command-injection patterns in request values, is best-effort and bypassable, and does not block by default.</li>
          <li>Coverage results were recorded on Linux x86_64. aarch64 is build-verified; the scenario matrix has not been re-run on arm64.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .totals { display: grid; gap: 1rem; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); margin: 0 0 2rem; }
  @media (min-width: 40rem) { .totals { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); } }
  .totals > div { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1rem 1.1rem; }
  .totals strong { display: block; font: 700 2rem/1 var(--display); color: var(--hot); }
  .totals span { font-size: .85rem; color: var(--muted); }
</style>
